<PubmedArticle><MedlineCitation Status="MEDLINE" Owner="NLM" IndexingMethod="Curated"><PMID Version="1">41186474</PMID><DateCompleted><Year>2025</Year><Month>12</Month><Day>16</Day></DateCompleted><DateRevised><Year>2026</Year><Month>01</Month><Day>27</Day></DateRevised><Article PubModel="Print-Electronic"><Journal><ISSN IssnType="Electronic">2325-8179</ISSN><JournalIssue CitedMedium="Internet"><Volume>56</Volume><Issue>12</Issue><PubDate><Year>2025</Year><Month>Dec</Month></PubDate></JournalIssue><Title>Ophthalmic surgery, lasers &amp; imaging retina</Title><ISOAbbreviation>Ophthalmic Surg Lasers Imaging Retina</ISOAbbreviation></Journal><ArticleTitle>One-year Real-world Outcomes and Durability With Faricimab in Patients With Diabetic Macular Edema.</ArticleTitle><Pagination><StartPage>726</StartPage><EndPage>734</EndPage><MedlinePgn>726-734</MedlinePgn></Pagination><ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3928/23258160-20250825-02</ELocationID><Abstract><AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">This study assessed real-world treatment patterns and 1-year outcomes among patients with diabetic macular edema (DME) initiating faricimab.</AbstractText><AbstractText Label="PATIENTS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">FARETINA-DME is a retrospective study using data from the IRIS&#xae; Registry for patients diagnosed with DME initiating faricimab from February 2022 to March 2023.</AbstractText><AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">Seven hundred eighty-six (786) treatment-naive patients (970 eyes) and 4,862 patients (6,728 eyes) previously treated with anti-VEGF therapy were included. Visual acuity improved by 4.5 &#xb1; 15.8 (mean &#xb1; SD) letters in treatment-naive eyes (<i>P</i> &lt; 0.001) and was maintained in previously treated eyes at injection-7. Central subfield thickness (CST) improved by -48.7 &#xb1; 82.7 &#x3bc;m in treatment-naive and -50.7 &#xb1; 101.1 &#x3bc;m in previously treated eyes (both <i>P</i> &lt; 0.0001); 42.3% and 43.8% had achieved/maintained C<i>ST</i> &#x2264; 280 &#x3bc;m at injection-7. Dosing frequency was reduced during the second 6 months (mean 1.9 to 2.7 injections) versus the first 6 months (3.4 to 3.9) of treatment.</AbstractText><AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">One-year outcomes among patients with DME initiating faricimab in clinical practice support the real-world effectiveness and extended durability of treatment.</AbstractText></Abstract><AuthorList CompleteYN="Y"><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Singh</LastName><ForeName>Rishi P</ForeName><Initials>RP</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>The Center for Ophthalmic Bioinformatics, Cole Eye Institute, Cleveland Clinic, Case Western Reserve University School of Medicine, Cleveland, Ohio.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Cleveland Clinic Martin Health, Cleveland Clinic Florida, Stuart, Florida.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Tabano</LastName><ForeName>David C</ForeName><Initials>DC</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Genentech, Inc, South San Francisco, California.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Borkar</LastName><ForeName>Durga S</ForeName><Initials>DS</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Duke University Eye Center, Durham, North Carolina.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Verana Health, San Francisco, California.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Ali</LastName><ForeName>Ferhina S</ForeName><Initials>FS</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Department of Ophthalmology, New York Medical College, Valhalla, New York.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Ahmed</LastName><ForeName>Ayesha</ForeName><Initials>A</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Genentech, Inc, South San Francisco, California.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Myrick</LastName><ForeName>Alayna</ForeName><Initials>A</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Verana Health, San Francisco, California.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Zwick</LastName><ForeName>Erin</ForeName><Initials>E</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Verana Health, San Francisco, California.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Downey</LastName><ForeName>Amanda</ForeName><Initials>A</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Hoffmann-La Roche Limited, Mississauga, Ontario, Canada.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Barteselli</LastName><ForeName>Giulio</ForeName><Initials>G</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Genentech, Inc, South San Francisco, California.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Leng</LastName><ForeName>Theodore</ForeName><Initials>T</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Byers Eye Institute at Stanford, Stanford University School of Medicine, Palo Alto, California.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author></AuthorList><Language>eng</Language><PublicationTypeList><PublicationType UI="D016428">Journal Article</PublicationType><PublicationType UI="D016448">Multicenter Study</PublicationType></PublicationTypeList><ArticleDate DateType="Electronic"><Year>2025</Year><Month>10</Month><Day>30</Day></ArticleDate></Article><MedlineJournalInfo><Country>United States</Country><MedlineTA>Ophthalmic Surg Lasers Imaging Retina</MedlineTA><NlmUniqueID>101599215</NlmUniqueID><ISSNLinking>2325-8160</ISSNLinking></MedlineJournalInfo><ChemicalList><Chemical><RegistryNumber>0</RegistryNumber><NameOfSubstance UI="D020533">Angiogenesis Inhibitors</NameOfSubstance></Chemical><Chemical><RegistryNumber>0</RegistryNumber><NameOfSubstance UI="D042461">Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor A</NameOfSubstance></Chemical><Chemical><RegistryNumber>0</RegistryNumber><NameOfSubstance UI="D011993">Recombinant Fusion Proteins</NameOfSubstanc